8.5M ranks in the top quartile among Energy peers, with revenue growing 50%/yr across its filed history. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Diamondback Energy, Inc. is a large-cap energy business with a $50.9B market cap on $15.0B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +16% over the past three years and +42% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 16% against a 8% cost of capital, a 8-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 2.3\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 5.2\u00d7.","Net dilution runs at 0.1% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insiders hold 24% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 170% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.7030209584281917},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.4) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $3754.6M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"The commodity cycle \u2014 revenue and free cash flow are ultimately hostage to a price the company does not set, and the long-run energy-transition arc adds a structural overhang.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"ESG-driven capital flight and stranded asset risk \u2014 tightening climate policy and investor mandates raise the cost of capital and risk leaving reserves permanently in the ground.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Geopolitical supply shocks \u2014 wars, sanctions, and OPEC decisions create volatility that no hedging programme can fully neutralise.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Growing faster than most Energy peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Can Diamondback Energy (NASDAQ:FANG) Sustain Its Operational Progress?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/energy/can-diamondback-energy-nasdaqfang-sustain-its-operational-progress","date":"2026-11-27","timestamp":1795806180.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.748,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Why Is Diamondback Energy (NASDAQ:FANG) Expanding Its Midland Basin Footprint?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/oil-gas/why-is-diamondback-energy-nasdaqfang-expanding-its-midland-basin-footprint","date":"2026-11-26","timestamp":1795719360.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.551,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Favorable Crude Oil Outlook: What Lies Ahead for COP, EOG & FANG?","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/energy/articles/favorable-crude-oil-outlook-lies-113500340.html","date":"2026-11-25","timestamp":1795606500.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.886,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["guidance"]},{"title":"Diamondback Energy (NASDAQ:FANG) Faces New Operational Challenges","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/oil-gas/diamondback-energy-nasdaqfang-faces-new-operational-challenges","date":"2026-11-24","timestamp":1795559820.0,"or